    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Safety\nIf you are sitting in an exit row\nand you cannot understand this\ncard or cannot see well enough\nto follow these instructions,\nplease tell a crew member.\nSicherheit\nSécurité\nSeguridad\nDC-10\noverwater\nUNITED\nAIRLINES\n270801205299\nWenn Sie neben einem Ausgang sitzen und Sie verstehen\nkein Englisch, bitte verständigen Sie die Flugzeugbesatzung\nSi vous êtes assis dans une rangée de sièges à côté d'une\nsortie et ne comprenez pas la langue anglaise, veuillez\nle dire à un membre de l'équipage.\nSi usted se encuentra sentado en una corrida de asientos\npróxima a una salida y no entiende el idioma Inglés como\npara seguir estas instrucciones por favor avisele a una\nazatata.\nEmergency exits are often heavy, awkward to lift, push,\npull, and maneuver when opening. Because of this, anc\nfor the safety of all passengers, Federal Law requires\nthat we only seat qualified passengers next to exits.\nIf you are sitting in an exit row, you may be asked to\nopen the exit and assist our crew in the event of an\nemergency. Please ask to be reseated if you:\n•Have a physical condition which may not be visible and\nwhich may prevent you from helping\n•Think you lack the strength, mobility, dexterity, or\nbalance required to open the exit and assist our crew.\n•Do not think you could reach the exit, open it, and get\nout quickly.\n•Believe the physical exertion required to open the exit\nwould injure you.\n•Are hearing impaired and could not hear commands\nfrom our crew.\n•Are not able to give oral commands to others.\n•Do not understand the instructions in this brochure.\n•Have other responsibilities (such as a small child to\ncare for which would prevent you from helping\n•Are less than 15 years old\n•Do not wish to help in this way.\nFederal regulations require all passengers,\nregardless of where they are sitting or their physical\ncondition, to review this card, for their safety.\nFollow these instructions, the directions of crew\nmembers, and placarded signs.\nWhen finished reviewing this card please return it\nto the seat pocket for our next customer.",
      "Do not use\n581808.\nBenutzen Sie nicht...\nNe pas utiliser ...\nNo use...\nLife Rafts\n7925\nSchlauchboote\nCanot pneumatique\nBalsas salvavidas\n2\nD0O0.\n#\nOder\nOu\nCA 360 2/92\nPrinted in the U.S.A.",
      "Take-off \u0026 landing\n98 49 44 4\nStart und Landung\nDécollage et atterissage\nDespegar y aterrizar\nBefore opening an exit,\nquickly look through\na window and check\noutside for the following:\nSmoke\nIf the smoke is so thick you\ncan not see out, direct\npassengers to other exits:\nDirect passengers\naway from aircraft.\nEmergency exits\nReWO\nNotausgänge\nSorties de secours\nSalidas de emergencia\nEXIT\nExit\n**0\nA7\nAusgang\nSortie\nSalida\nNo smoking\nRauchen verboten\nDéfense de fumer\nNo fumar\nFire\nDebris/\nObstructions\nIf there is fire outside the\naircraft direct passengers\nto other exits.\nIf there are obstructions or\nmetal debris outside, direct\npassengers to other exits.\nA\nB\nOxygen\nSauerstoff\nOxygène\nOxigeno\nCheck that the slide has properly inflated and is in good condition.\nCheck that the slide has properly inflated and is in good condition.\nCopyright © Aero Safety Graphics Inc. 1992. All Rights Reserved."
    ],
